{"availability":"available","full":"nautilus-os/GUST","name":"GUST","description":"GUST is a powerful, modern web proxy designed by the Nautilus Labs dev team for especially restrictive environments. It's a fully static, single HTML file allows it to be downloaded, shared, and distributed with ease, and with no reliance on serviceworkers, GUST can be used without the need to host it on an admin-blockable website.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":119,"forks":236,"created":"2026-04-18T04:36:27Z","updated":"2026-10-03T16:37:43Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gust-browser.vercel.app/","topics":["dinguschan","goguardian-bypass","html","lightspeed-bypass","maintained","pr0xy","proxies","proxies-for-school","proxies-for-school-chromebook","proxy","proxy-site","school","school-proxy","securly-bypass","self-hosted","unblockable","unblocked","unblocker","web-proxy"],"demo":"https://gust-browser.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:16.971Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:16.971Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:16.971Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:35:16.971Z","stars":119,"forks":236}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GUST is a full-featured web proxy that lives entirely inside a single HTML file, allowing you to use it without any setup, hosting, or terminal access. It was built by the Nautilus Labs team to be a replacement for every single other proxy out there, and to put an end to school blocked proxies once and for all.","Every single web proxy out there relies on something called a Service Worker, a background script that intercepts network requests before they reach the browser. It's an integral part of any other web proxy you use, allowing the proxy to communicate with its server and proxy your requests, but Service Workers ALWAYS require a live server to function. That means traditional proxies only work when hosted at a specific URL. Block that URL, and the proxy is dead. You're probably already familiar with the cat-and-mouse game between you and your admin, where someone makes a link, it gets used for a…","School network filters, admin installed extensions (think Securly, Lightspeed Systems, Securly, Linewize, Blocksi, etc.) and admin-controlled browsers (like Chromebook MDM policies) are very good at exactly this. Your school maintains blocklists, with specific sites added every day to this list of sites you can't access. Many filtering extensions also have more advanced features, where they read a links metadata to detect proxy patterns and automatically add them to the blocklist. An even higher number of these extensions control what can run in the background, which is a big achilles heel…"],"features":["✅ It can run as a local file (file://), with no server and no domain to block","✅ It can be hosted anywhere static files work: GitHub Pages, Vercel, Netlify, a USB drive, a Google Doc, a Google Site, etc.","✅ It can be hosted on JSDelivr or CDN sites, because the site can be loaded through one SVG file","✅ It has no Service Worker to kill, because it never registered one","✅ It can be renamed, embedded in an iframe, or wrapped in another HTML file, giving the filter nothing to latch onto"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nautilus-os/GUST/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2a81a051f874b03c1f9895974a1896b7b43b6b36983ef33a621875ef3c3343d5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.074Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.074Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"GUST is a full-featured web proxy that lives entirely inside a single HTML file, allowing you to use it without any setup, hosting, or terminal access. It was built by the Nautilus Labs team to be a replacement for every single other proxy out there, and to put an end to school blocked proxies once and for all.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nautilus-os/GUST/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"You can self-host a WISP server or use a public one, and GUST supports server switching in settings.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nautilus-os/GUST/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"2a81a051f874b03c1f9895974a1896b7b43b6b36983ef33a621875ef3c3343d5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nautilus-os/GUST/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.075Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T16:37:43Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nautilus-os/GUST/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.075Z","hash":"2a81a051f874b03c1f9895974a1896b7b43b6b36983ef33a621875ef3c3343d5","originalBytes":12632,"storedBytes":12632,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["proxy","gust","file","html","server","every","inside","page","svg","they","wisp","browser","built","features","just","service","single","sites","web","websocket","work","any","block","built-in","fixes","pages","through","url","used","works","font","hosted","links","network","one","option","project","request","school","script","settings","webassembly","what","which","workers","already","another","bar","because","before","blocking","compiled","css","day","entire","even","extensions","file.","filtering","gets","http","iframe","labs","lane","language","libcurl.js","like","most","nautilus","only","other","out","panel","pdf","pdf.js","proxied","proxies","requests","run","site","support","there","things","version","viewer","when","without","worker","access.","address","admin","again","all.","allowing","api","assorted","background","basically","been","being","blob","bookmarks","broken","browser.","bug","bugs","called","came","cat-and-mouse","client","clock","compatibility","customizable","data","developer","did","dinguschan","documentation","download","dude","editor","else","engine","etc.","experience","feature","feedback","files","filter","first","framework","full","game","gave","github","google","history","hobby","hosting","how"